# Building a knowledge graph: the gate before extraction and the check after it (36 cases).
#
# extract_gate: a chunk of a corpus + what is being extracted -> extract | skip. The skips
#               are what a real crawl is mostly made of: navigation, cookie notices, tables
#               of contents, legal footers, generalities. Hard positives: a footer that does
#               name a company, and a heading list that does name a ruling, because the
#               question is whether an instance is there, not whether the chunk is prose.
# edge:         a candidate triple against the chunk it was extracted from -> supported |
#               reversed | unsupported. Both mentions appear in the text in every case, so
#               this measures meaning only; the literal check that catches an invented
#               mention runs in code before any call and is covered by the unit tests.
#               Hard negatives: co-occurrence without the relation, a different relation
#               between the same two entities, and the relation stated the other way round.
#
# Single-annotator, authored 2026-09-24. Content is Spanish without accents.
{"id": "eg-01", "point": "extract_gate", "input": {"looking_for": "personas y empresas, y la relacion entre ellas", "kinds": ["persona", "empresa", "relacion"], "chunk": "La sociedad Inversiones Delta S.A. fue constituida en Ciudad de Panama en 2011. Su socio unico es Mario Reyes Castillo, quien figura ademas como representante legal desde la fecha de constitucion."}, "expected": "extract"}
